        "lrc": "[00:00.000] 作词 : JOHN BETTIS/Richard Carpenter\n[00:00.000] 作曲 : JOHN BETTIS/Richard Carpenter\n[00:00.000]When I was young I'd listen to the radio\n[00:07.889]Waiting for my favorite songs\n[00:13.419]When they played I'd sing along\n[00:18.406]It made me smile\n[00:25.023]Those were such happy times and not so long ago\n[00:30.913]how I wondered where they'd gone\n[00:36.176]But they're back again just like a long lost friend\n[00:42.592]all the songs I loved so well\n[00:47.700]Every shalalala every wo'wo\n[00:54.085]Still shines\n[00:59.548]Every shing-a-ling-a-ling\n[01:02.618]That they're starting to sing\n[01:05.260]So fine\n[01:10.543]When they get to the part\n[01:13.740]Where he's breaking her heart\n[01:16.400]It can really make me cry\n[01:20.857]Just like before\n[01:26.983]It's yesterday once more\n[01:29.784](shoobie do lang lang)\n[01:39.772]Looking back on how it was in years gone by\n[01:45.483]And the good times that I had\n[01:51.064]Makes today seem rather sad\n[01:55.808]So much has changed\n[02:02.671]It was songs of love that I would sing to then\n[02:08.319]and I'd memorize each word\n[02:13.427]Those old melodies still sound so good to me\n[02:19.814]As they melt the years away\n[02:24.956]Every shalalala every wo'wo still shines\n[02:36.336]Every shing-a-ling-a-ling\n[02:39.646]That they're starting to sing\n[02:42.303]So fine\n[02:47.648]All my best memories come back clearly to me\n[02:53.448]Some can even make me cry\n[02:57.773]Just like before\n[03:04.083]It's yesterday once more\n[03:06.552](shoobie do lang lang)\n[03:10.286]Every shalalala every wo'wo still shines\n[03:21.963]Every shing-a-ling-a-ling\n[03:24.753]That they're starting to sing\n[03:27.572]So fine\n[03:32.715]Every shalalala every wo'wo still shines.\n"
